source	Thomas Aquinas, Summa Theologica I, tr. Fathers of the English Dominican Province (1920), q.2 a.3
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 17611, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/17611
class	inference
at	S13	Therefore it is necessary to arrive at a first mover
fault	two unstated steps: that the regress of movers cannot be infinite is asserted, not shown (a series of movers moved by others may have no first); and the first mover is identified with God without argument
reference	A. Kenny, The Five Ways (1969), ch. 2
known	canon
